There is a couple of issues to keep in mind:
* `primesieve` for getting previous / next prime may be too slow due to the need of initialization / rewinding;
* with `proof=False` (ie. without certification), the fastest option would be using gmplib's [functions `mpz_nextprime` and `mpz_prevprime`](https://gmplib.org/manual/Number-Theoretic-Functions)

@vbraun Under the cover of innocent-sounding PR titles such as "Fix release dist workflow"
